      "metadata": {
        "split_group": "conflict_pending"
      },
      "narrative": "The consumer disputed a late-payment month directly with the CRA and the intake packet was valid. The CRA notified the furnisher on the third business day and forwarded the consumer's payment receipt. The consumer's receipt, the CRA file, and the furnisher response show materially conflicting dates for the same payment. The CRA has not yet resolved the conflict, has not completed the reinvestigation, has not determined whether the item should be verified, deleted, or modified, and has not sent final results. The case is routed to manual review because of the material date conflict and conflicting documents. No reseller, reinsertion, consumer-statement, or direct-furnisher branch applies.\n",
      "provenance": "authored",
      "structured_fields": {},
      "title": "Clear conflict leaves substantive disposition undetermined"
    },
